.TH RENDER_LIST "1" "2026-10-22" "mod_tile v0.8.1"
.\" Please adjust this date whenever revising the manpage.
.SH NAME
render_list \- renders a list of map tiles by sending requests to a rendering daemon.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B render_list
.RI [ OPTIONS ]\ <\  "render.list"
.SH DESCRIPTION
This manual page briefly documents the
.B render_list
command.
.PP
.B render_list
is a helper utility that takes a list of map tiles from STDIN and sends the requests to a rendering daemon.
.SH OPTIONS
This program follows the usual GNU command line syntax, with long
options starting with two dashes (`-').
A summary of options is included below.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\^\-all
Render all tiles in given zoom level range instead of reading from STDIN.
.TP
.BI \-c " CONFIG" "\fR,\fP \-\^\-config=" CONFIG
Specify a `renderd.conf` file from which to load various option values rather than specifying via command line.
.br
The following options will be set (if present); however, they can be overridden if also specified:
.RS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\^\-socket
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\^\-num\-threads
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\^\-tile\-dir
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\^\-min\-zoom
.TP
.BR \-Z ", " \-\^\-max\-zoom
.RE
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\^\-force
Render tiles even if they seem current.
.TP
.BI \-m " MAP" "\fR,\fP \-\^\-map=" MAP
Render tiles in this map (default is 'default').
.TP
.BI \-l " LOAD" "\fR,\fP \-\^\-max\-load=" LOAD
Sleep if load is this high (default is '16').
.TP
.BI \-s " SOCKET|HOSTNAME:PORT" "\fR,\fP \-\^\-socket=" SOCKET|HOSTNAME:PORT
Unix domain socket name or hostname and port for contacting renderd (default is '/run/renderd/renderd.sock').
.TP
.BI \-n " NUM" "\fR,\fP \-\^\-num\-threads=" NUM
The number of parallel request threads (default is '1').
.TP
.BI \-t " TILE" "\fR,\fP \-\^\-tile\-dir=" TILE_DIR
Tile cache directory (default is '/var/cache/renderd/tiles').
.TP
.BI \-z " ZOOM" "\fR,\fP \-\^\-min\-zoom=" ZOOM
Filter input to only render tiles greater than or equal to this zoom level (default is '0').
.TP
.BI \-Z " ZOOM" "\fR,\fP \-\^\-max\-zoom=" ZOOM
Filter input to only render tiles less than or equal to this zoom level (default is '20').
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\^\-help
Print out a help text for \fBrender_list\fR.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\^\-version
Print out the version number for \fBrender_list\fR.
.PP
If you are using \fB\-a\fR or \fB\-\-all\fR, you can restrict the tile range by adding these options:
.br
(please note that tile coordinates must be positive integers and are not latitude and longitude values)
.RS
.TP
.BI \-g " LATITUDE" "\fR,\fP \-\^\-min\-lat=" LATITUDE
Minimum latitude.
.TP
.BI \-G " LATITUDE" "\fR,\fP \-\^\-max\-lat=" LATITUDE
Maximum latitude.
.TP
.BI \-w " LONGITUDE" "\fR,\fP \-\^\-min\-lon=" LONGITUDE
Minimum longitude.
.TP
.BI \-W " LONGITUDE" "\fR,\fP \-\^\-max\-lon=" LONGITUDE
Maximum longitude.
.TP
.BI \-x " X" "\fR,\fP \-\^\-min\-x=" X
Minimum X tile coordinate.
.TP
.BI \-X " X" "\fR,\fP \-\^\-max\-x=" X
Maximum X tile coordinate.
.TP
.BI \-y " Y" "\fR,\fP \-\^\-min\-y=" Y
Minimum Y tile coordinate.
.TP
.BI \-Y " Y" "\fR,\fP \-\^\-max\-y=" Y
Maximum Y tile coordinate.
.RE
.PP
If you are not using \fB\-a\fR or \fB\-\-all\fR, send a list of tiles to be rendered from STDIN in \fB"X Y Z"\fR format, e.g.:
.RS
.PP
0 0 1
.br
0 1 1
.br
1 0 1
.br
1 1 1
.RE
.PP
The above would cause all 4 tiles at zoom 1 to be rendered.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR renderd (1)
